19. How Do You Ensure Event Order Is Not Broken?
(This is often asked in banking projects.)
Answer
Use message key.
 
producer.send(
 
new ProducerRecord<>(
 
   "payments",
 
   accountId,
 
   event));
 
``
 
All events for the same account go to the same partition.
Interview Answer
I use business key partitioning such as AccountId or CustomerId to ensure related events are always written to the same partition, preserving ordering. [Java_Inter...heat_Sheet | PDF], [Java Inter...one place | Word]
20. How Do You Achieve Exactly-Once Processing?
Answer
Use:
 
enable.idempotence=true
 
acks=all
 
and producer transactions.
 
producer.initTransactions();
 
producer.beginTransaction();
 
producer.send(...);
 
producer.commitTransaction();
 
``
 
Kafka supports transactions and idempotent producers for exactly-once processing. [Interview...reparation | Word], [DataEngine..._Interview | Word]
